Environment Setup
Step 1 — Create conda environment:
bash
conda create -n signify python=3.10
conda activate signify

⚠️ Important: Install PyTorch manually (Step 2) BEFORE running pip install -r requirements.txt. If you run requirements.txt first, pip will install the CPU version of PyTorch instead of the CUDA version.

Step 2 — Install PyTorch with CUDA:
bash
pip install torch==2.5.1 torchvision==0.20.1 torchaudio==2.5.1 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121
Step 3 — Install core libraries:
bash
pip install opencv-python==4.9.0.80 mediapipe==0.10.14 numpy==1.26.4
Step 4 — Install training libraries:
bash
pip install scikit-learn==1.4.2 matplotlib==3.8.4 seaborn==0.13.2 Pillow==10.3.0 tqdm==4.66.4
Step 5 — Install API and utilities:
bash
pip install fastapi>=0.124.1 uvicorn>=0.34 python-multipart>=0.0.9 kaggle==1.6.14 python-dotenv>=1.0.1 aiofiles==23.2.1
Step 6 — Install speech libraries:
bash
pip install SpeechRecognition==3.10.4 gTTS==2.5.1 pygame==2.5.2 pydub==0.25.1
Step 7 — Install Whisper:
bash
pip install git+https://github.com/openai/whisper.git
Step 8 — Install Ollama:
•	Download and install from https://ollama.com/download — Windows installer
•	After installation open a new terminal and pull the model:
bash
ollama pull llama3.2
Step 9 — Install Ollama Python client:
bash
pip install ollama
Step 10 — Verify installation:
python
import torch
import cv2
import mediapipe
import ollama

print("PyTorch:", torch.__version__)
print("CUDA available:", torch.cuda.is_available())
print("GPU:", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if torch.cuda.is_available() else "None")
print("OpenCV:", cv2.__version__)
print("MediaPipe:", mediapipe.__version__)
print("Ollama:", ollama.__version__)
print("All systems ready")

